    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FOR SALE BY ONLINE AUCTION THURSDAY, 29TH OCTOBER 2026 \n\nIMPRESSIVE TWO-STOREY DETACHED RESIDENCE REQUIRING COMPLETION ON A CHOICE SITE AT REDHILLS, CO. CAVAN\n\nSmith Property are delighted to present this substantial detached residence extending to approximately 266.4 sq.m. (2,867 sq.ft.), situated on a large and prominent site in the highly regarded residential area of Redhills.\n\nThis impressive two-storey red brick home offers purchasers an excellent opportunity to complete and finish a substantial family residence to their own taste and specification. The property is currently unfinished and requires full completion of internal and external works, including the provision and connection of essential utilities and services such as water, wastewater treatment, electricity and broadband.\n\nDesigned to provide generous living accommodation, the property has the potential to become a superb family home in a peaceful yet convenient location. The spacious site offers excellent privacy and ample outdoor space while enjoying a prominent position close to the village and local amenities.\n\nRedhills is a popular residential location renowned for its strong community spirit and quality of life. The property is within easy reach of local schools, shops, sporting facilities and community services. Both Cavan Town and Cootehill are approximately 15 20 minutes away, providing access to a wider range of amenities and employment centres.\n\nRegistered with Cavan County Council under Planning Application No. 2560741, this property presents an appealing opportunity for builders, developers or private purchasers seeking to create a bespoke family home in a desirable countryside setting. Prospective purchasers should review the planning documentation and auction legal pack for details of the permitted development, associated conditions and outstanding completion requirements.\n\nViewing by appointment through Smith Property.\n\nAUCTION PROCESS IMPORTANT INFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\n\n\nPlease familiarise yourself with the auction process before bidding. The property will be offered for sale by online auction on Thursday, 29th October 2026 via the Offr platform.\n\nBidder Security and Payment\n\n\nA 1,000 bidder security payment, together with the applicable registration fee, must be paid in advance to enable you to bid on auction day. \n\nIf you are unsuccessful, the 1,000 bidder security payment will be refunded in full.\n\nIf you are the successful bidder, you become immediately contractually bound at the fall of the hammer. The balance required to bring your contract deposit to 10% of the purchase price must be paid immediately. This deposit is non-refundable, subject to the auction contract conditions.\n\nBidder Registration\n\n\nIntending bidders must pre-register through the Offr widget on the subject property listing at www.smithproperty.ie at least 24 hours before the auction.\n\nRegistration deadline: Wednesday, 28th October 2026 at 3:00pm, or 24 hours before the scheduled auction time, whichever is earlier.\n\nAll registration requirements and advance payments must be completed within the required timeframe.\n\nLegal Documentation\n\n\nRegister through your Offr account to access the auction legal documentation. Some documents may only become available closer to the auction date. Once registered, you will receive an alert when these become available to download.\n\nWe strongly advise all prospective purchasers to have their solicitor review the complete legal pack and auction conditions before bidding.\n\nIMPORTANT NOTICE\n\n\nThese particulars do not constitute a formal offer. They are provided for information purposes only and give a general description of the property. They do not form part of any resulting contract and should not be relied upon as statements or representations of fact.\n\nWhilst every care has been taken in their preparation, neither Smith Property nor the vendor accepts liability for their accuracy. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by personal inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of these particulars.\n\nNo person employed by Smith Property has authority to make or give any representation or warranty in relation to this property."
      },
